<===> README.md
Like dart-sass, a namespace can't be interpolated (also not for variables,
e.g. `#{"m"}.$x`), and the default namespace of `@use` (the last path
segment of the url) must be a valid identifier (e.g. not for "dir/").
<===>
================================================================================
<===> interp_mid/input.scss
a {b: x#{1}.$x}
<===> interp_mid/error
Error: Interpolation isn't allowed in namespaces.
  ,
1 | a {b: x#{1}.$x}
  |       ^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 1:7  root stylesheet
<===>
================================================================================
<===> interp_var/input.scss
a {b: #{"m"}.$x}
<===> interp_var/error
Error: Interpolation isn't allowed in namespaces.
  ,
1 | a {b: #{"m"}.$x}
  |       ^^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 1:7  root stylesheet
<===>
================================================================================
<===> use_digit/input.scss
@use "a/1foo";
a {b: 1foo.$x}
<===> use_digit/error
Error: The default namespace "1foo" is not a valid Sass identifier.

Recommendation: add an "as" clause to define an explicit namespace.
  ,
1 | @use "a/1foo";
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 1:1  root stylesheet
<===>
================================================================================
<===> use_dir/input.scss
@use "dir/";
a {b: c}
<===> use_dir/error
Error: The default namespace "" is not a valid Sass identifier.

Recommendation: add an "as" clause to define an explicit namespace.
  ,
1 | @use "dir/";
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^
  '
  input.scss 1:1  root stylesheet
